  "Number": 19,
  "Question": "If the product \\[\\dfrac{3}{2}\\cdot \\dfrac{4}{3}\\cdot \\dfrac{5}{4}\\cdot \\dfrac{6}{5}\\cdot \\ldots\\cdot \\dfrac{a}{b} = 9,\\] what is the sum of \\(a\\) and \\(b?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(11\\)",
    "B": "\\(13\\)",
    "C": "\\(17\\)",
    "D": "\\(35\\)",
    "E": "\\(37\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Each denominator after the first matches the numerator immediately before it. The pattern also tells us that the final denominator is \\(b=a-1\\). Combining the fractions exposes the cancellation:\n\\[\n\\frac{3\\cdot4\\cdots a}{2\\cdot3\\cdots(a-1)}=\\frac a2.\n\\]\nAll canceled factors are positive, so the cancellation is valid. Since the product equals \\(9\\), we have \\(a=2\\cdot9=18\\). Therefore \\(b=17\\), and\n\\[\na+b=18+17=\\boxed{35}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
